      "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"@solvo/token-burn-mcp\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"MCP server for token burn — proxies user-pasted Anthropic API key to real token usage data. Works with Claude Code Desktop via stdio.\",\n  \"main\": \"index.js\",\n  \"type\": \"commonjs\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"token-burn-mcp\": \"./index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node index.js\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"^1.29.0\"\n  },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=18.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"mcp\",\n    \"modelcontextprotocol\",\n    \"claude-code\",\n    \"token-burn\",\n    \"anthropic\",\n    \"api-key\"\n  ],\n  \"license\": \"MIT\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "sha": null,
      "content_sha256": "d281f81ad3a5d61fb9c69e2b099bf974352a9fd13056bb403e934230586d1994",
      "score": 100,
      "content": "# @solvo/token-burn-mcp\n\nMCP server that retrieves real token burn data from Anthropic's API using a user-provided API key. Designed for use with Claude Code Desktop.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. User pastes their Anthropic API key (starts with `sk-ant-...`)\n2. The MCP server makes a minimal `max_tokens: 1` request to Anthropic's `/v1/messages` endpoint\n3. Real token usage (`input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `total_tokens`) is extracted from the response\n4. Returns burn data including estimated burn rate\n\nThe API key is used only for the single live request and is never stored.\n\n## Install for Claude Code Desktop\n\n### Option 1: Install globally\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g @solvo/token-burn-mcp\n```\n\n### Option 2: Install as a project dependency\n\n```bash\nnpm install @solvo/token-burn-mcp\n```\n\nThen add to your MCP settings (`~/.claude/settings.json` or project `.claude/settings.json`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"token-burn\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"@solvo/token-burn-mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Option 3: Run directly via npx\n\n```bash\nnpx @solvo/token-burn-mcp\n```\n\n## Configure in Claude Code Desktop\n\nAdd to your Claude Code settings file (`~/.claude/settings.json`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"token-burn\": {\n      \"command\": \"node\",\n      \"args\": [\"/absolute/path/to/node_modules/@solvo/token-burn-mcp/index.js\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nOr if using the global install:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"token-burn\": {\n      \"command\": \"token-burn-mcp\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Usage\n\nOnce installed and configured, use the `get_token_burn` tool in a Claude Code session:\n\n```\n/burn <your-anthropic-api-key>\n```\n\nOr via the tool call:\n\n```\nTool: get_token_burn\napi_key: [REDACTED]\n```\n\n## Response\n\nReturns:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"authenticated\": true,\n  \"input_tokens\": 1200,\n  \"output_tokens\": 45,\n  \"total_tokens\": 1245,\n  \"rate_limit_remaining\": \"99\",\n  \"estimated_burn_rate\": \"871.5 tokens/min\",\n  \"quota_warning\": false\n}\n```\n\n## Error handling\n\n- Invalid key (doesn't start with `sk-`) → descriptive error\n- Invalid or expired key → descriptive error\n- API timeout → descriptive error\n- Network error → descriptive error\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js >= 18.0.0\n- `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` ^1.29.0\n\n## License\n\nMIT",
      "redaction_applied": true,
      "redaction_reasons": [
        "secret_assignment"
      ]
